// ─── Operators Feature ─────────────────────────
// Operators (arithmetic, comparison, logical, bitwise) are built into the
// expression parser's precedence climbing algorithm in parser/expressions.fg.
// They produce core AST nodes (Expr.Binary, Expr.Unary) directly — no
// feature-specific side table or parse handler is needed.
//
// This feature module exists for registry completeness: it declares that
// operators are a recognized feature, but registers no parse handlers.
// Type checking and codegen for operators are handled by the core
// expression pipeline.

use core.registry.register_feature_meta

// ─── Registration ────────────────────────────────
// Operators produce core Expr.Binary/Expr.Unary nodes directly in
// the expression parser's precedence climbing — no separate handlers needed.

register_feature_meta("operators", "Arithmetic & Comparison Operators", "wip")
